<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO chief sees European bank mergers.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO chief sees European bank mergers.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO NV managing board chairman Jan Kalff said on Wednesday he expected far-reaching concentration among small local banks in Europe as a result of the introduction of a single European currency.</p>
<p>He told a business luncheon that European economic and monetary union (EMU) would produce stiffer competition among European banks, putting even stronger pressure on margins.</p>
<p>In the face of the competition, they could choose between such options as being a niche bank, regional bank, pan-European bank with limited services and pan-European universal bank with a complete range of services.</p>
</text>
